      "text": "Let the integer be denoted by \\( n \\). According to the problem, when \\( n \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5, and then sum these remainders.\n\nFirst, consider the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\div 3 \\) has a remainder of 1, we have:\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, consider the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\div 5 \\) has a remainder of 2, we have:\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we sum the remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
