      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by expressing the given condition mathematically. We know that when an integer \\( x \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be written as:\n\n\\[ x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\]\n\nThis means that \\( x \\) can be expressed in the form:\n\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 \\]\n\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. We will consider each part separately.\n\n### Step 1: Find the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3\nWe substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder when divided by 3:\n\n\\[ x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. We do this by performing the division:\n\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\n### Step 2: Find the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5\nWe substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder when divided by 5:\n\n\\[ x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. We do this by performing the division:\n\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\n### Step 3: Find the sum of the remainders\nWe have found that the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1, and the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2. To find the sum of these remainders, we add them together:\n\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
