      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's denote the integer by \\( n \\). According to the problem, when \\( n \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. Let's start with the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3.\n\nFirst, substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder when divided by 3:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\div 3 \\) gives a quotient of 2 and a remainder of 1, we have:\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nSo,\n\\[ n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThis means the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. Again, substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder when divided by 5:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\div 5 \\) gives a quotient of 1 and a remainder of 2, we have:\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSo,\n\\[ n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThis means the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of these remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
